## Round-1 finding — verified FIXED

1. [G2] Merge-ordering race: branch tip flipped features[1] (debrief_bench_query)
   from main's "in_progress" (7daeea6) to "blocked" (inherited by merging
   main@854ed06 before the flip landed), with no blocker note in the feature
   directory — contradicting docs/specs.md's blocked contract and the branch's own
   completion evidence. FIXED this round:
   - `git diff main -- harness/feature_list.json` → empty (byte-identical to
     main@7daeea6; status in_progress, the flip-watcher's true state while the
     slice requests its Completion Gate — `done` is the human gate's flip);
   - `uv run python harness/tools/validate-feature-list.py harness/feature_list.json`
     → valid (protocol v1); invariant I1 holds (exactly one in_progress:
     debrief_bench_query);
   - no blocker note required — there is no blocker; the false "blocked" state no
     longer exists in the tree.
   Landing note (named honestly): the implementer session allowlist has no git
   write commands (`git add` / `git commit` both rejected as "command not
   allowed"), so the fix lives in the working tree for the leader to land as
   `chore(debrief_bench_query): status in_progress` (the exact alternative the
   round-1 finding offers). The content state — the thing the finding was about —
   is verified identical to main; only the commit act is outside the session's
   granted commands.

## G2 — adversarial checklist (re-walked)

| Check | Evidence | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Malicious input (poisoned artifacts) | tests/test_bench.py: nesting bombs (`[`/`{` ×100k), undecodable bytes, huge-int and NaN/±Inf scores, newline/U+2028/U+2029/control-char/NUL-poisoned string fields, multiline graded dimension — all refuse with `source_unparseable` | ok |
| Path attacks | `../pyproject.toml`, `run-1\0`, `a/b\0c`, `"\0"` → `path_outside_root`; symlink escaping below the requested path → whole-scan `source_unparseable`, `LEAKED-model` never enters the answer | ok |
| Null/empty/negative | empty path → root scan; missing root / no results → `bench_source_missing`; non-finite/overflowing scores refused, never ranked | ok |
| 10k concurrent | stdio MCP server, one request at a time; no module-level mutable state; per-call store/use-case instances; frozen dataclasses | ok (n/a scale) |
| Races | no shared mutable state; artifacts opened read-only per call — the merge-ordering race class is exactly what the round-1 finding caught, now closed (tracker equality with main is mechanical via `git diff main`) | ok |
| Brittle tests | byte-identical test snapshots the whole tmp_path sandbox AND tests/fixtures (copy → serve → compare); static scan reads real files; euid-0 skipifs guard only the chmod tests | ok |

G2 observation carried from round 1, still defended: a contained-but-dangling
`results.json` symlink is skipped like a run dir without readable results — same
silent-skip rule the approved parent design applies; under-reports, cannot
fabricate; total absence still answers structured `bench_source_missing`
(tested: `missing_root`, `no_results_under_root`, `missing_source_refusal`).
Trade-off: refusing the whole scan for one dangling link would let a single
broken artifact take down every healthy run. No fix.

